    <article>
      <div class="key-points">
        <h2>The short version</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Vodka is engineered for <strong>neutrality</strong>. Baijiu is engineered for <strong>aroma</strong>. That single design goal explains every other difference.</li>
          <li>Baijiu ferments grain in a <strong>solid</strong> state with a microbial starter; vodka ferments a liquid wash and distils it repeatedly.</li>
          <li>Baijiu carries far higher levels of <strong>congeners</strong> — the aroma compounds that also make hangovers worse.</li>
          <li>Vodka is served cold and mixed. Baijiu is served at room temperature, in small cups, with food.</li>
          <li>They are not interchangeable in cocktails, but baijiu substitutes well for gin, aged rum, or peated whisky — not for vodka.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <nav class="toc" aria-label="On this page">
